sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch08-11> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Slight changes in conditions of life benefit organisms, and crosses between slightly different members of the same species give vigour and fertility to offspring, whereas greater changes and wider crosses tend to cause sterility.";
    dc:type "empirical-generalization";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Slight changes of conditions and slight crosses both increase vigour and fertility";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter VIII, “Hybridism”; section “Parallelism between the effects of changed conditions of life and crossing”. Scope: plants and animals generally"
}
